; Issue #3265: --strict-commodity, like --strict, must only add checking.
; A `commodity` directive used to mark its commodity known only under one
; of these options, and a known commodity takes no display precision from
; price entries (#2481), so the option dropped the cents that $ otherwise
; learns from the price below.

commodity $
commodity AAPL
account Assets:Brokerage
account Equity:Opening

P 2024/01/01 AAPL $150.125

2024/01/02 Buy
    Assets:Brokerage    10 AAPL
    Equity:Opening

test bal -X $
           $1501.250  Assets:Brokerage
          $-1501.250  Equity:Opening
--------------------
                   0
end test

test bal -X $ --strict-commodity
           $1501.250  Assets:Brokerage
          $-1501.250  Equity:Opening
--------------------
                   0
end test

test bal -X $ --strict
           $1501.250  Assets:Brokerage
          $-1501.250  Equity:Opening
--------------------
                   0
end test
